                <pb facs="0577" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg565"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.34553B/23a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kennan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-20T19:00:00-04:00">November 20,
                            1943—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2108. The British Embassy has asked the Department, in view of the fact that
                    British support is to be furnished in your forthcoming negotiations, that it be
                    furnished the nature of facilities you will request. The Embassy has been told
                    that the Department is not fully informed on the subject and that considerable
                    latitude has been given you. The Embassy replied that perhaps you could
                    communicate to Sir Ronald Campbell the requests you propose to make at this
                    time.</p>
                <p>You are requested nevertheless to furnish the Department by cable an outline of
                    the requests you will make at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
